 ## Overview
-Mega-NeRF is a training configuration for Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) designed to accelerate training and reduce model query costs for large-scale scenes. It differs from standard NeRF by using a single shared Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) for both coarse and fine sampling stages, which reduces model size and saves 25% of model queries per ray by reusing coarse outputs during the fine rendering stage [S1].
+Mega-NeRF is a training configuration for Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) designed to accelerate training and reduce model query costs for large-scale scenes [S1]. It differs from standard NeRF by using a single shared Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) for both coarse and fine sampling stages, which reduces model size and saves 25% of model queries per ray by reusing coarse outputs during the fine rendering stage [S1].
 
